ot to  stay before i went home  to watch that because i i just couldn't  miss it it was  amazing to watch i think i know what  you're talking about  um for each of you again i would imagine  making this was just awesome  but when you think back on the shoot is  there like a day or two  that you will always remember forever  and like do you remember what it was  about that day  there was um the last day of filming i  remember me and  kylie when we were done with everything  craig  like put us on stage and he thanked us  in front of everyone  and it was just a really nice moment and  it was really it was really sweet and  kind  yeah and everybody was exchanging gifts  and saying goodbye  a lot of people were crying especially  me i was crying the whole ride home  i didn't i didn't want to go that's why  i love  filming and i love acting so much  because i realize just how much i want  to do it  um it was amazing uh i'm a big fan of  ruth carter who did the costumes in the  movie  i'm just curious for each of you what  was it like working with ruth  and hypothetically what did you borrow  from set because i know you wouldn't  have stolen anything  i loved all the costumes it was so much  fun walking into my trailer every day  and seeing a brand new  outfit or a brand new dress or a costume  it was so much fun to see that and all  the different accessories  she even had you know i could take in  the accessory that  the accessories that would go in the  hair and everything that we would wear  it was so much fun  trying on a bunch of different outfits  that was a lot of fun i couldn't even  choose a favorite because they were all  so cool you know like the fighting  outfits and  the ceremonial type things that we would  wear while we're sitting on their own  they were all amazing  yeah it was a joy to work with ruth  she's so great at her job and  um you know as an actor  costumes have such a big impact on how  you play your character  and really can help you you know  si